  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Contour on an open run that is picked on the stock no longer rides the run with the tool centre. The tool centre now stands one tool radius plus the stock to leave off the run, on the side that Side names:\n\n- Outside: the side of the run without stock.\n- Inside: the stock's side of the run.\n- Auto: the side away from the part.\n\nFiles:\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_run_stock.rs` (new): `contour_open_run_sided`. It reads the stock and part sections at each cut level and offsets the run with the #1777 `offset_run`. It checks the ride against the part with `clear_of_part`. Climb keeps the stock on the right of the tool (#1555).\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_run_side.rs`: `material_side` takes the body name for its messages (\"part\" or \"stock\"). The part messages are not changed. Some helpers are now `pub(super)`.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: the Contour selection arm calls `contour_open_run_sided` for runs that are not part runs. It gives the raw Side, the stock facets and the setup's parts (`keep_parts`).\n- `crates/app/src/operation/selection.rs`: the note \"Side does not apply to open runs\" shows only when no pick is on the stock.\n- `docs/decisions/1928-stock-open-run-offset.md`: the decision.\n\nRefused by name, never guessed:\n\n- Inside or Outside when no stock is beside the run at a cut level.\n- Auto when there is no part, when the part is on both sides of the run, or when the part changes sides between levels.\n- A tool beside the run that would enter the part.\n- An offset that is not positive or that folds onto itself.\n\n## Readings\n\nFixture: part 40 x 40 x 10, stock 70 x 70 x 10, tool D10. Pick: the north edge of the stock (y = 35).\n\n| Case | Before (main d1484f02a) | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Side Auto | 0.0000 mm off the line (on y = 35) | 5.000 mm, on y = 40, 0 warnings |\n| Side Outside | 0.0000 mm | 5.000 mm, on y = 40 |\n| Side Inside | 0.0000 mm | 5.000 mm, on y = 30 |\n| Stock to leave 0.5, Outside | 0.0000 mm | 5.500 mm |\n| No part, Auto | cut on the line | refused, names Inside and Outside |\n| Stock 44 x 44, Inside | cut on y = 22, 3 warnings | refused, \"cuts the part\" |\n\nThe issue comment has the full readings and the list of callers of `contour_along_chain`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/contour_stock_run.rs` (5 tests): `a_stock_run_is_cut_one_radius_off_the_line_by_its_side`, `stock_to_leave_moves_the_stock_run_further_off`, `a_stock_run_posts_clean`, `auto_on_a_stock_run_with_no_part_is_refused_by_name`, `a_stock_run_whose_tool_enters_the_part_is_refused_by_name`. Before the fix, 4 of the 5 failed.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_run_stock_tests.rs` (8 tests): each side at one radius (D6, 3.000 mm within 0.001 mm, both run directions), stock to leave, climb direction, and each refusal.\n\n## Gate\n\n- Motion suites of the quick gate (lib + 50 test binaries): pass (798 s).\n- App suites of the quick gate (lib + 117 test binaries): pass, except `operations::threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit` on base d1484f02a. That failure is the known red main of #1924 (a 3D Pocket reach refusal), fixed by PR #1925. After a merge of `origin/main` (9d52dfb30), `operations` passes (120 passed, 6 ignored), and so do `contour_stock_run` (5) and `contour_open_side` (2).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean, before and after the merge.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI. No screenshot: the change has no UI layout change. The selection note text changes only for stock picks.\n- A tilted frame: a picked selection with a tilt is refused before this arm.\n- Golden CL and NC files: none changed.\n\nChangelog: Contour on an open edge of the stock now cuts beside the edge, one tool radius plus stock to leave off it, on the side that Side names, instead of on the edge. A side that cannot be read is refused by name.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1928\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
